endobj
461 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (    Self-compassion involves relating to oneself with kindness rather than harsh judgment during failure or suffering. Kristin Neff's model includes three components: self-kindness \(versus self-judgment\), common humanity \(recognizing suffering as universal rather than isolating\), and mindfulness \(balanced awareness rather than over-identification\). Self-compassion predicts resilience and wellbeing without undermining motivation.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
462 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Practice: Use the self-compassion break: When suffering, place hand on heart and say: "This is a moment of suffering. Suffering is part of life. May I be kind to myself." Write a compassionate letter to yourself from the perspective of a loving friend.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
463 0 obj
<<
