<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (    Resilience is the capacity to maintain or quickly restore functioning following adversity. It involves adaptive coping \(problem-focused and emotion-focused strategies\), optimism, meaning-making, self-compassion, and social support. Resilience is trainable rather than fixed.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
499 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Practice: Develop resilience systematically: build stress tolerance gradually \(hormesis\), cultivate optimistic explanatory style \(viewing setbacks as temporary, specific, and external\), maintain social connections, practice meaning-making \(finding purpose in challenges\), and develop multiple coping strategies.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
