/S /P
/E (    Divergent thinking involves generating multiple possible solutions, perspectives, or interpretations from a single starting point. It's measured through fluency \(quantity of ideas\), flexibility \(diversity of categories\), originality \(uniqueness\), and elaboration \(detail\). Divergent thinking is trainable and essential for creativity.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
609 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
